.th LOCK II 5/4/78
.sh NAME
lockon, lockoff \*- lock/unlock process in memory
.sh SYNOPSIS
(lockon = 49.: not in assembler)
.br
.bd "sys lockon"

.bd "lockon()"

(lockoff = 50.: not in assembler)
.br
.bd "sys lockoff"

.bd "lockoff()"
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Lockon
locks the calling process in low memory
(\ after suitable core shuffling\ ).
.s3
.it Lockoff
unlocks the calling process.
.s3
Locking a process in memory when there is not enough unlocked memory
left to run anything else is obviously undesirable.
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
Error bit (c-bit) is set if the user is not the super-user.
From C, a -1 value indicates an error.
